<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000016> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000016> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "disposition" .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000019> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000019> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "quality" .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000040> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000040> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "material entity" .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OGMS_0000031> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "A disposition (i) to undergo pathological processes that (ii) exists in an organism because of one or more disorders in that organism." .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OGMS_0000031> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "Native BioPortal hierarchy: OGMS" .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OGMS_0000031> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OGMS_0000031> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "disease" .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OGMS_0000031> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000016> .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OGMS_0000045> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "A material entity which is clinically abnormal and part of an extended organism. Disorders are the physical basis of disease." .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OGMS_0000045> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "Native BioPortal hierarchy: OGMS" .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OGMS_0000045> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OGMS_0000045> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "disorder" .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OGMS_0000045> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000040> .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OGMS_0000063> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "The totality of all processes through which a given disease instance is realized." .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OGMS_0000063> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "Fallback evidence copied losslessly from the master review CSV" .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OGMS_0000063> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OGMS_0000063> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "disease course" .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OGMS_0000086> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "A pattern of signs and symptoms that typically co-occur." .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OGMS_0000086> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "Native BioPortal hierarchy: OGMS" .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OGMS_0000086> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OGMS_0000086> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "syndrome" .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OGMS_0000086> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000019> .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OGMS_0000102> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "A disorder that involves some structural damage that is immediately caused by a catastrophic external force." .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OGMS_0000102> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "Native BioPortal hierarchy: OGMS" .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OGMS_0000102> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OGMS_0000102> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "At the scale of organism (as opposed to the cellular scale or the population scale), an injury is typically the result of a catastrophic event. Consider the implications of making 'injury' a subtype of 'disorder'.\n\nNote: Adopted subtype of disorder, and injury can occur at the scale of organism down to cellular level." .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OGMS_0000102> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "injury" .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OGMS_0000102> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OGMS_0000045> .
